# Owner loop

Allen develops from Cursor on the web. The phone is Obtainium. Android
Studio is not the install path. Do not sit idle waiting for a laptop.

## Shipping line

- `trunk` is the only sitting line. `main` is gone. Do not recreate it.
- GitHub needs a temporary head to open a PR. That branch is a vehicle,
  not a line of work. Squash-merge into `trunk` the same turn the JVM
  gate is green, then **delete the remote branch**. Leftover `cursor/*`
  heads are a process defect.
- One packet, one throwaway branch off current `trunk`, one PR into
  `trunk`, then the branch is gone.
- Branch names: `cursor/<short-slug>-b87f`.
- JVM (`./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` + `assembleDebug`) is the push
  gate. Run it here, on Cursor.
- After merge, the phone gets **Temper Debug** from a GitHub
  pre-release. Tag `debug-live-YYYY-MM-DD` (or `-2` on a same-day
  drop). Attach `PersonalTrainer-*-debug.apk`. Obtainium is what the
  owner taps. Do not tell the owner to open Android Studio.
- **Do not use GitHub-hosted runners as a test lane.** Do not ask the
  owner to click a red X, lift Actions billing, or grant Checks /
  Actions scopes so an agent can read workflow logs. The yaml may
  stay. Ignore it. Cursor JVM + Obtainium are how we test.

## Continue after merge

Start the next packet as soon as the current one is on `trunk` and the
JVM gate is green. Do not wait for a phone check. Do not leave the
previous vehicle branch sitting.

## No accidental overlap

Before cutting a branch, list every path already changed on an **open**
PR against `trunk`.

- None of those paths are needed → cut from `trunk`. Independent. Phone
  check and merge in any order.
- A path is already owned → **stack** on that PR's branch. Do not start
  a second edit of the same file from `trunk`.
- `docs/ROADMAP.md` is the one file every packet is allowed to touch in
  a few lines. Last merge wins. Do not use that exception for Kotlin.

A stacked PR includes the packets under it. Say so in the body. Merge
the tip only — not each layer as if they were strangers.

## Phone check

Obtainium, not Studio. Add `https://github.com/sinura7/PersonalTrainer`,
include pre-releases, prefer `PersonalTrainer-*-debug.apk`. That install
is **Temper Debug** (`com.sinura.personaltrainer.debug`) — a second icon
and a second database. Gym-floor **Temper** stays on the signed
`PersonalTrainer-<version>.apk` entry. Never point the gym-floor
Obtainium app at a `*-debug.apk`. Never run
`connectedDebugAndroidTest` on the release `applicationId`.

## Current program

`docs/FOUNDATION_PROGRAM.md` and `docs/architecture/` are current law.
Jobs 1–6 are historical. Do not open a CI / billing / runner packet.

## Still not these jobs

A sixth tab, Library or Goals as a tab, an LLM-as-author, package or Drive-folder rename, Job 2 P5
sex, catalog seed, `fallbackToDestructiveMigration`, GitHub-hosted
runners as a test lane. A waiting PR is not permission to open a
different job.

**Room v3 won’t is superseded** for the one signed Phase 5 cutover
(`docs/architecture/ADR-010-schema-reset-migrations.md`). Do not invent
a `TrainerDatabase` v3 during polish. Do not reset after the foundation
freeze.

Jobs 1–6 are code-done on `trunk`. Phone gates stay the owner's.
